      <section id="faq" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">8. FAQ</h2>

        <div class="space-y-5">
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">Can I sell a product that isn't in the catalog yet?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              No. You must first register it in the catalog and wait for it to be verified
              and activated. Once active, you can create a listing against it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">What's the difference between registering a product and creating a listing?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              Registering a product adds it to the shared catalog — the description of the
              product itself. Creating a listing is your store's specific offer: price,
              stock, and shipping. You register once; you list as many times as you want.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">How long does verification take?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              Most submissions are reviewed within a few business days. Complex ones may
              take longer. You'll be notified when your product is activated or denied.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">Can I edit a product after it's been activated?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              No. Once activated, product details are admin-only. If you spot a mistake,
              contact support — an admin can make the correction.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">What happens to my listings if a product is disabled?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              Existing listings continue to work. The product simply stops appearing as an
              option for new listings. If the product is later re-enabled, it becomes
              available again.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">I found a duplicate. What should I do?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              Report it to <a href="mailto:sales@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a> with
              both product references. Admins will merge or remove the duplicate.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">Can another vendor list against the product I registered?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-1">
              Yes. The catalog is shared. Once a product is active, any vendor can list it.
              This is by design — the catalog is a common reference, not a vendor-private
              asset.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

